    "created_at": "2015-09-02T21:05:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-02T21:05:29Z",
    "body": "In particular:\n- All three of these should be exported.  They're all useful terms that you want to be able to link to.\n- All three need an id.\n- All three need to be \"distinguishable\", which means they need distinct text and/or type and/or for value. Currently, they're all \"dfn\" type definitions.  (I think I want to add a \"header\" dfn type, which'll at least take care of the Origin header.)  That means at least two of them need a \"for\" value namespacing them.  I recommend a `for=\"url\"` on the url origin, and a `for=\"resource\"` on the resource origin.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
